    "summary": "Recreational scene of two men dancing; single-page painting on an album folio. Right man plays a stringed instrument while the other (facing directly opposite) holds the scarf hung around his neck. Both men are dressed in short cloth (revealing their legs) with decorations tied below each knee. Feathered hats adorn their heads. Album contains 44 paintings and drawings, mostly of Persian costumes and animals with some drawings by Kaempfer.\r\nInk and opaque watercolour on paper. Album is bound in brown leather with gold gilt decoration. Inside covers have marbled paper.",
